UID:261022YFls1WjUjEKRK2lBSvd_gA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a hands-on workshop where tradition meets artistry
 . Alissa Kaplan\, maker and founder of Zizland Atelier\, will guide you th
 rough the craft of broom making as you create your own Wrapped Hawk Tail W
 hisk—a beautiful and functional hand broom with deep roots in American f
 olk tradition.\n\nIn this 3-hour class\, you’ll learn:\n\n• A brief hi
 story and uses of hand brooms\n\n• Traditional Shaker/Appalachian bindin
 g and wrapping techniques\n\n• How to select and prepare broomcorn for a
  whisk\n\n• Step-by-step guidance to craft your own wrapped Hawk Tail Wh
 isk to take home\n\nWhether you’re drawn to heritage crafts\, seasonal r
 ituals\, or simply love working with your hands\, this workshop offers a m
 eaningful way to connect with timeless skills and leave with something use
 ful and beautiful.\n\nSome hand strength is required. Material and tools w
 ill be supplied.
LOCATION:Gather Sebastopol
URL:https://gathersebastopol.com/products/the-art-of-broom-making
