BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://salsadancemarin.com/cumbia/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:4-Week Beginner Cumbia with Mireille: October 27 – November 17
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T193000
UID:2610230XciMAC4Zkym82KSrdPcDw
DESCRIPTION:**4-week\, Tuesdays at 6:30 PM**\n\nOCTOBER 27 – NOVEMBER 17
 \n\n**Feel the Rhythm with Cumbia**\n\nReady to master the “Step of the 
 Soul”? Join us for a high-energy cumbia class where we dive into the hea
 rt of Latin America’s most infectious dance. Whether you have two left f
 eet or you’re a dance floor regular\, this class will get you moving wit
 h confidence.\n\n**Mireille will guide you through:**\n\n**4-Week Beginner
  Cumbia Series Program**\n\nWeek 1 – Foundations & Rhythm\n\n• Introdu
 ction to cumbia music and timing\n\n• Basic steps ( tropical and sonider
 a basics )\n\n• Understanding the beat ( quick quick slow – quick quic
 k slow )\n\n• Intro to partner connection (closed/open hold) ⸻\n\nWeek
  2 – Footwork Development + cumbia Basic Turns\n\n• Review of basic st
 ep\n\n• Cumbia prep for turns\n\n• Traveling basics (moving around the
  floor)\n\n• Intro to basic cumbia turns .\n\n• Partner timing and fra
 me basics\, partner work combination. ⸻\n\nWeek 3 – Styling & Partner 
 Patterns\n\n• Review turns\n\n• Adding simple styling (arm movement\, 
 body rhythm)\n\n• Cross-body lead variation (beginner-friendly)\n\n• S
 mooth transitions between moves\n\n. Partner work combination. ⸻\n\nWeek
  4 – Putting It All Together\n\n• Review all footwork and patterns\n\n
 • Combining moves into a short sequence\n\n• Musicality: dancing with 
 the music\n\n• Confidence and flow on the dance floor\n\n• Social danc
 ing practice + mini recap\n\nImportant Details\n\n**No dance experience re
 quired:** Whether you’ve never danced before or it’s been a while\, yo
 u’re welcome here!\n\n**No partner necessary:** Come solo or bring a fri
 end—either way\, you’ll have plenty of opportunities to dance.\n\nPlea
 se wear **non-marking shoe soles:** This helps us keep our dance floor in 
 great condition.\n\nCome join us and discover the joy of cumbia. We can’
 t wait to see you on the dance floor.\n\nDate & Time: **Tuesdays \, 6:30 p
 m**\n\n**4 week course\,** OCTOBER 27 – NOVEMBER 17\n\nInstructor: **Mir
 eille Ruiz** Born and raised in Mexico City\, she grew up dancing and list
 ening to Latin Music as part of her culture including Cumbia\, Banda\, ran
 chera\, quebradita\, etc. she learned her first following Techniques\, dan
 cing with her father in every family fiesta. she has a background in Mexic
 an folklore\, Jazz\, tap dancing and gymnastics\, she also is a percussion
 ist\, drummer and Montessori Teacher.\n\nShe grew up performing since she 
 the age of 4. Bay Area bachata and cumbia dance instructor\, Mireille has 
 been teaching dance\, performing\, leading dance teams\, around USA events
 \, dance festivals\, congresses since 2008\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highwa
 y #8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking s
 hoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin 
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cumbia/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
