SUMMARY:Author Event: Her Womanhood of Mine by Haley Hutchinson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T180000
UID:261014BC1YjXqmDE23-U8qAtzVEg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special event with Haley Hutchinson\, author of 
 Her Womanhood of Mine. This event is free\, but we appreciate your RSVP be
 low so we can plan for your attendance. ABOUT THE BOOK Haley Hutchinson’
 s Her Womanhood of Mine is a chronicle of a girlhood painted by the tastes
 \, pains\, and folds of the body. It is a love letter to place\, a yearnin
 g for the past\, and an eventual understanding of the raw grittiness of ex
 istence. These poems sing with the blue messiness of coming into one’s s
 elf\, the growing and waning of relationships\, and the appreciation for s
 implicity. Rich with experiences both familiar and nuanced\, Her Womanhood
  of Mine invites us to sit with ourselves\, to notice\, to muddle\, to blo
 om. "Her Womanhood of Mine is a luminous record of becoming: a book that t
 urns domestic detail into devotion." — Isabelle Correa\, Author of Good 
 Girl and Other Yearnings "The tender speaker of Her Womanhood of Mine reck
 ons with the hurts of girlhood\, longing for a relationship to womanness b
 eyond the surveilling force of another’s gaze. But this is not a speaker
  who refuses the world. This book is fragrant—“wine-soaked\,” “alg
 al\,” “drop of orange blossom\,” “molasses and grit”—with the 
 sensuous material of being alive. Despite the grief of what does not last\
 , in Haley Hutchinson’s Her Womanhood of Mine\, it is the romance of bec
 oming that endures." — Patrycja Humienik\, author of We Contain Landscap
 es ABOUT THE AUTHOR Haley Hutchinson \\(she/her\\) is a poet\, editor\, an
 d bookseller originally from the Mendocino Coast of California. A graduate
  of Middlebury College and the Columbia Publishing Course\, Haley now resi
 des in San Francisco where she is a bookseller at Russian Hill Bookstore a
 nd editor at Gal Pal Media. Her work has been previously featured in the B
 erkeley Review\, Gather\, the Anthology of Women Poets of Mendocino County
 \, and elsewhere. She is the author of Her Womanhood of Mine \\(Green Writ
 ers Press\, 2026\\).
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/2881828752177076/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.gunbun.com/event/schnucks-wine-dinner/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Schnucks Wine Dinner with Jeff Bundschu
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T210000
UID:260824O470BKruPE64u9E7lHuF_g
DESCRIPTION:Schnucks Wine Dinner with Jeff Bundschu\n\nWe invite you to jo
 in Jeff Bundschu at Schnucks Des Peres in St. Louis MO on Wednesday Octobe
 r 28th from 6-9pm for a special wine dinner. It will be a culinary experie
 nce you won’t want to miss\, delicately paired with exceptional wines an
 d their friendly staff.\n\nFROM THE HOST\n\nJoin us for an exclusive five-
 course culinary journey featuring the exceptional cool-climate estate wine
 s of Gundlach Bundschu\, Sonoma’s oldest continuously family-owned winer
 y. The evening features sixth-generation vintner and special guest Jeff Bu
 ndschu\, who will share his personal stories\, deep-rooted passion\, and d
 istinctively vibrant approach to California winemaking. As each meticulous
 ly paired course unfolds\, you will gain firsthand insight into the unique
  terroir of their historic Rhinefarm estate\, their sustainable wine-growi
 ng philosophies\, and the meticulous crafting process that has defined the
  Bundschu family legacy for nearly 170 years.\n\nMENU\n\nGreeter: Gundlach
  Bundschu 2025 Gewurztraminer | Gundlach Bundschu 2025 Sauvignon Blanc \\}
  Goat Cheese Tart with Asian Pear and Star Fruit | Gundlach Bundschu 2024 
 Chardonnay \\} Seared Scallops with Green Apple Beurre Blanc | GunBun Pino
 t Noir 2022 \\} Smoked Turkey Roulade with Wild Rice | Gundlach Bundschu M
 ountain Cuvee 2023 \\} Cocoa Rubbed Rack of Lamb with Plum Reduction\, Swe
 et Potato Puree and Haricot Vert | Gundlach Bundschu 2021 Cabernet Sauvign
 on \\} Basque Chocolate Cheesecake with Blackberries\n\nCan’t make it? P
 lease share with your local foodies!\n\nBOOK NOW
LOCATION:Gundland Bundschu Winery
URL:https://www.gunbun.com/event/schnucks-wine-dinner/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
