X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.deadmansdinner.com", "Press Democrat": "http://www.deadmansdinner.com", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/dead-mans-dinner/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.deadmansdinner.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Dead Man's Dinner
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T230000
UID:2609110RFypztdA0SHtcBaUD63wg
DESCRIPTION:Beyond the mist lies a secret devil's den where outlaws\, harl
 ots\, and the scalliest of wags gather to feast beneath the redwoods.\n\nT
 ake cover under timbered canopy of Rio Nido Lodge and step inside the sump
 tuous sanctuary of Dead Man’s Dinner—an immersive evening of decadent 
 dining and world-class cabaret just in time for Halloween weekend.\n\n​F
 or one night only\, be transported to a hidden heathen's haven\, alive wit
 h flickering candles and shadowed walkways while distant murmurs fill the 
 air. As the veil thins and Mischief Night unfolds\, you’ll gather under 
 the stars and indulge in a lavish feast paired with bespoke craft spirits 
 while roving scoundrels and spellbinding burlesque unfold all around you.\
 n\nOne part secret society. One part dinner theater. A wholly unforgettabl
 e experience: Dead Man’s Dinner invites you to leave the modern world be
 hind and join the Captain’s Court for one extraordinary night inspired b
 y pirate mythos\, dark fairytales\, and maritime lore.\n\nTickets on-sale 
 now. Capacity for this immersive experience is limited.\n\n**Dinner item
 s and signature cocktail menu to be announced.**\n\nFor questions and inqu
 iries regarding Dead Man's Dinner\, please call: (213) 650-0803 or email u
 s at deadmansledger@gmail.com
LOCATION:Rio Nido Lodge
URL:http://www.deadmansdinner.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108773802?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Hot Buttered Rum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T200000
UID:260910fICsI2Hb_U609awrFGJOcg
DESCRIPTION:“Stunning instrumental and vocal virtuosity.” – Relix Ma
 gazine\n\n“Few things rejuvenate the soul like a warm fireside drink aft
 er an exhausting day in the snow. Hot Buttered Rum has that effect. Their 
 original songs are instantly familiar and inviting\, and their easygoing v
 ersions of timeless classics \\(the Beatles\, Hank Williams\\) belie the i
 ntricacy of the arrangements.” –San Francisco Chronicle\n\nHot Buttere
 d Rum lives for a good time\, and a mindful recklessness settles in whenev
 er these five guys step on stage. From Anchorage to Miami\, the group’s 
 onstage chemistry fuels the lovefest that is a live Butter show. Rooted in
  the trajectory of west coast bluegrass\, Hot Buttered Rum plays what has 
 been described as California’s own acoustic music.\n\nHBR’s years of t
 ouring have given the band the chance to work and play with a wide cross-s
 ection of musicians\, people like Peter Rowan\, Phil Lesh\, Chris Thile\, 
 Brett Dennen\, and Robert Earl Keen. Seasoned veteran Steve Berlin \\(Los 
 Lobos\\)\, acoustic guru Mike Marshall\, and left-coast rocker Tim Bluhm \
 \(Mother Hips\, Nicki Bluhm\\) have all produced studio albums for the ban
 d. Each guided HBR towards the next step in its evolution. It’s a sound 
 that is tough to describe and easy to love\, and it has found its way to t
 he most prestigious pop\, folk\, and bluegrass stages in the country: Tell
 uride\, Newport\, Bonnaroo\, Strawberry\, Hardly Strictly\, Kate Wolf\, Ho
 rning’s Hideout\, String Summit\, Grey Fox\, Merlefest\, All Good\, High
  Sierra\, Wakarusa\, and many more.\n\nThe next step in Butter’s evoluti
 on involves recording three 6-song EPs\, each focusing on a part of music 
 that Hot Buttered Rum loves and is inspired by\, and each with a different
  producer. The first EP was recently recorded with Railroad Earth’s Tim 
 Carbone and will be released this fall. The second will be a collection of
  Ralph Stanley old school bluegrass standards\, to be recorded in Septembe
 r with producer Sally Van Meter. The third will be Hot Buttered Rum’s la
 tenight throwdown music\, to be recorded in November with SCI’s Kyle Hol
 lingsworth. Together\, the three collections of songs will explore Butter
 ’s roots and express Butter’s present passions.\n\nAt the center of Ho
 t Buttered Rum is the enduring camaraderie of old friends. The band was co
 nceived on a backpacking trip of high school and college buddies in the Hi
 gh Sierra. What was dreamed up on mountaintops and around campfires has fo
 und its way into the hearts\, minds\, and bodies of thousands.
LOCATION:New Family Farm
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108773802?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
