X-SOURCE-ID:cmosc
X-SOURCE:Children's Museum of Sonoma County, North Bay Bohemian
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T103000
DTSTAMP:20260904T203614Z
CREATED:20260902T170119Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T203614Z
UID:10020073-1793440800-1793442600@www.cmosc.org
SUMMARY:Cuentos con Ritmo (Stories with Rhythm)
DESCRIPTION:Cuentos con Ritmo (Stories with Rhythm)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCuentos con Ritmo | Cuentos * Música * Movimiento \n\n\n\nPresentado por Colors of Spanish \n\n\n\nCuentos con Ritmo es una oportunidad única semanal para niños de 1 a 5 años y sus familias\, el cual aporta alegría\, comprensión y aprecio por la lengua española a toda la comunidad. Durante Cuentos con Ritmo\, los pequeños visitantes y sus familias participan de forma lúdica en historias interactivas con música y movimiento fortaleciendo nuestra diversa comunidad y entusiasmo por la lengua meta. \n\n\n\nCuentos con Ritmo es presentado por Guadalupe Tausch en colaboración con la organización que fundó\, Colors of Spanish. Originaria del estado de Guanajuato en México\, tiene una maestría en español con énfasis en la adquisición de una segunda lengua para la primera infancia y continúa sus estudios enfocada en la primera infancia especializándose en la adquisición de idiomas a través de la música/movimiento. Colors of Spanish ofrece talleres para profesores\, bibliotecarios y cuidadores y organiza programas de cuentos en español con música y movimiento en escuelas\, bibliotecas y museos locales. www.colorsofspanish.org \n\n\n\nCuentos con Ritmo | Cuentos * Música * Movimiento \n\n\n\nPresented by Colors of Spanish \n\n\n\nCuentos con Ritmo (Stories with Rhythm) is a weekly one-of-a-kind opportunity for children ages 1-5 and their families that brings joy\, understanding and appreciation for the Spanish language to Spanish- and English-speaking speakers alike. During Cuentos con Ritmo\, young visitors and their families playfully engage in interactive stories with music and movement that build community and an excitement for language! \n\n\n\nCuentos con Ritmo is presented by Guadalupe Tausch in collaboration with the organization she founded\, Colors of Spanish. Originally from the state of Guanajuato in México\, she has a master’s degree in Spanish with emphasis in second language acquisition for early childhood and continues her study of childhood and music/movement trainings. Colors of Spanish provides workshops for teachers\, librarians and caregivers and hosts Spanish story time with music & movement programs at local schools\, libraries\, and museums. www.colorsofspanish.org \n\n\n\nDesigned for kids 1-5\, families\, and siblings. \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nGenerously sponsored by RCU and the SABA Foundation.
URL:https://www.cmosc.org/event/cuentos-con-ritmo-stories-with-rhythm-8-copy/2026-10-31/
CATEGORIES:Toddlers,Spanish Storytime,Special Guests,Special Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.cmosc.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/spanish_storytime.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T170000
UID:261004WpoSanx5u064FIoPqDkpCQ
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
