ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,460,460/717_Friedman_Bennett_playing_sax-2_460x460.r
 ev.1788902572.jpg
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:The concert will feature guitarist Randy Vincent\, bassist Rob
 b Fisher\, drummer Kendrick Freeman\, and saxophonist Bennett Friedman.Ran
 dy Vincent has been teaching jazz guitar at Sonoma State University since 
 1981. He has performed with Bobby Hutcherson\, Joe Henderson\, and Dizzy G
 illespie. Vincent has authored six jazz guitar books\, published by Sher M
 usic Co.  Bassist Robb Fisher toured and recorded with the legendary Cal T
 jader for more than six years\, anchoring Tjader's Grammy Award-winning al
 bum\, "La Onda Va Bien\," and Grammy-nominated album\, "Gozame Pero Ya." H
 e has also worked extensively with and recorded for jazz and Latin artists
 \, including Chet Baker\, Art Pepper\, Carmen McRae\, Tania Mara\, Clare F
 ischer\, Rob Schneiderman\, Eddie Marshall\, Dick Whittington\, and Anita 
 O'Day.Kendrick Freeman has a background in both drum set and hand drums\, 
 having studied with American artists and musicians from Ghana\, Congo\, an
 d the Caribbean\, with an emphasis on Haitian music. Freeman leads a jazz 
 ensemble at Sonoma State University.  Saxophonist Bennett Friedman has per
 formed at the Monterey Jazz Festival\, the Stanford Jazz Workshop\, the Sa
 n Jose Jazz Festival\, the Healdsburg Jazz Festival\, the Monterey Bay Blu
 es Festival\, and the Russian River Jazz Festival. He has been featured as
  a soloist with Frank Sinatra\, Rosemary Clooney\, Natalie Cole\, and Marv
 in Gaye. Friedman has taught Jazz Studies at Santa Rosa Junior College sin
 ce 1977. He is the recipient of a National Endowment for the Arts grant fo
 r jazz composition.  Concert proceeds benefit the SRJC Foundation Jazz Stu
 dies Fund.  General Admission $15 &amp\; student/senior $10 (at the door o
 nly).  Parking on campus is $4.For more information\, visit the SRJC Music
  Events website. (https://music.santarosa.edu/events)
LAST-MODIFIED:20261013T163543Z
LOCATION:Newman Auditorium - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23985-bennett-friedman-jazz-quart
 et
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The concert will feature guitarist Randy
  Vincent\, bassist Robb Fisher\, drummer Kendrick Freeman\, and saxophonis
 t Bennett Friedman.</p><p><strong>Randy Vincent</strong> has been teaching
  jazz guitar at Sonoma State University since 1981. He has performed with 
 Bobby Hutcherson\, Joe Henderson\, and Dizzy Gillespie. Vincent has author
 ed six jazz guitar books\, published by Sher Music Co.</p><p>  Bassist <st
 rong>Robb Fisher</strong> toured and recorded with the legendary Cal Tjade
 r for more than six years\, anchoring Tjader's Grammy Award-winning album\
 , "La Onda Va Bien\," and Grammy-nominated album\, "Gozame Pero Ya." He ha
 s also worked extensively with and recorded for jazz and Latin artists\, i
 ncluding Chet Baker\, Art Pepper\, Carmen McRae\, Tania María\, Clare Fis
 cher\, Rob Schneiderman\, Eddie Marshall\, Dick Whittington\, and Anita O'
 Day.</p><p><strong>Kendrick Freeman</strong> has a background in both drum
  set and hand drums\, having studied with American artists and musicians f
 rom Ghana\, Congo\, and the Caribbean\, with an emphasis on Haitian music.
  Freeman leads a jazz ensemble at Sonoma State University.</p><p>  Saxopho
 nist <strong>Bennett Friedman</strong> has performed at the Monterey Jazz 
 Festival\, the Stanford Jazz Workshop\, the San Jose Jazz Festival\, the H
 ealdsburg Jazz Festival\, the Monterey Bay Blues Festival\, and the Russia
 n River Jazz Festival. He has been featured as a soloist with Frank Sinatr
 a\, Rosemary Clooney\, Natalie Cole\, and Marvin Gaye. Friedman has taught
  Jazz Studies at Santa Rosa Junior College since 1977. He is the recipient
  of a National Endowment for the Arts grant for jazz composition.</p><p>  
 Concert proceeds benefit the SRJC Foundation Jazz Studies Fund.</p><p>  Ge
 neral Admission $15 &amp\; student/senior $10 (at the door only).<br />  P
 arking on campus is $4.</p><p><a href="https://music.santarosa.edu/events"
  target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more information\, visit the SRJC Musi
 c Events website.</a></p>
