SUMMARY:Hunting for the Snark Illustrations
DTSTART:20261106T000000
DTEND:20261106T000000
UID:6fa4de43938bb6a18f5c4acabce8bf2e@jacklondonpark.com
DESCRIPTION:Step inside the House of Happy Walls Museum for a fascinating 
 exploration of Jack London’s photographic journey aboard the Snark. Jack
  London always referred toThe Cruise of theSnark (1911) as an “illustrat
 ed book.” The pictures were central to his authorial vision of the voyag
 e to the South Pacific that he and Charmian London embarked on in April of
  1907. Maddeningly\, in the process of preparing the manuscript ofThe Crui
 se of theSnark for publication\, Macmillan & Co. made a hash of the author
 ’s
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park\, 2400 London Ranch Road\, Glen E
 llen\, CA 95442
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-speaker-series-amy-tucker
X-SOURCE:Jack London State Historic Park
