BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/rituals-of-care-buddhist-chant-and-culture-ch1d26/?lang=en", "Press Democrat": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/rituals-of-care-buddhist-chant-and-culture-ch1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/rituals-of-care-buddhist-chant-and-culture-ch1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Rituals of Care: Buddhist Chant and Culture
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T150000
UID:2610124TsF0sXRn0u3nhC4VwHKtg
DESCRIPTION:Learn to chant with Chenxing Han and Trent Walker\n\nWhat is t
 he role of chant in Buddhist practice? How does it shape communities of be
 longing and cultures of care?\n\nDuring this daylong\, we will engage in a
  variety of chanting practices from across the Buddhist world\, with a spe
 cial emphasis on the Theravāda tradition as transmitted in mainland South
 east Asia. We’ll explore the musical and textual dimensions of chant\, a
 s well as its ritual possibilities. Our charge as a group will be to embod
 y chant as an expression of care for ourselves\, our loved ones\, and the 
 world.\n\nThere will be time to reflect on questions of voice\, language\,
  and lineage. Nearly every Buddhist throughout history has engaged in reci
 tation and other practices of aspiration\, concentration\, and devotion. O
 ur day together invites us into kinship with them as we\, too\, experience
  the healing resonances of these practices.\n\nAll are warmly welcome to p
 articipate\; no previous chanting experience is required.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/rituals-of-care-buddhi
 st-chant-and-culture-ch1d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
