BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/loswappo26", "Press Democrat": "https://sec.regfox.com/loswappo26"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/loswappo26"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Senderos: Los Wappo en Wilikos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T104500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T130000
UID:261017BjPe56NN3EyFYHI26N7ALw
DESCRIPTION:\\[Translated to English below\\] Aprende acerca de las histor
 ias y tradiciones de la tribu Wappo\, una de las tribus originarias de est
 a área\, en esta caminata familiar de 2 millas. Nos reuniremos en el esta
 cionamiento del granero blanco (el White Barn) y caminaremos el sendero Me
 adow mientras escuchamos acerca de la historia cultural de los Wappo en un
 a de sus aldeas ancestral\, Wilikos\, hoy en día parte de Sugarloaf. \n\
 nEvento gratuito\; requiere registración. Hay transportación disponible 
 gratuita dentro de un radio de 20 millas al parque para familias que la ne
 cesiten. Para detalles y registración\, visita EVENT LINK\n\nAlternativam
 ente\, llama a Mario (707-387-4087)\, Alma (707-247-5767)\, entre martes y
  sábado) o escríbenos a senderos@sonomaecologycenter.org. ¿No puedes ac
 ompañarnos ese día? ¡Guarda la fecha el 5 de diciembre para más aventu
 ras!\n\nSenderos Naturales es parcialmente respaldado por una beca de Park
 s California.\n\nFotografía cortesía de Alma Shaw\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\n\nLearn about the history and traditions of the Mishewal Wappo T
 ribe\, one of the original groups to live in this area. On this family hik
 e\, will walk approximately 2 miles along the Meadow trail while we listen
  to the cultural history of the Wappo peoples in one of their ancestral vi
 llages called Wilikios\, today found in Sugarloaf.\n\nThis event is planne
 d around a primarily Latino audience and will be conducted in Spanish. Fam
 ilies from underrepresented groups are welcome to join. Free transportatio
 n available within a 20 mile radius of the park for families in need. For 
 questions\, please email senderos@sonomaecologycenter.org.\n\nThis event i
 s partially supported by Route to Parks\, a project of Parks California.\n
 \nPhoto courtesy of Alma Shaw
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/loswappo26
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partners"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art FREE Nov 7-8 Bank of America Museums o
 n Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T170000
UID:261022GUszNd268UenDhTXssOc1w
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is November 7-8. \n\nWith Thanksgiving and winter just around
  the corner\, the late fall season means just one thing: it’s the perfec
 t time for some indoor fun at your local museum! The Sonoma Valley Museum 
 of Art has exciting exhibits including brand new installation The Real-Lif
 e Art History of M. Louise Stanley\, an exhibit sponsored by Bank of Ameri
 ca that celebrates a unique Bay Area Figurative artist for her wildly imag
 inative narratives and distinctly female perspective\, shaped by her keen 
 observations of everyday life and setting her apart from her male contempo
 raries. The exhibit features Sanley’s large-scale acrylic paintings\, go
 uache and watercolor works on paper\, sculptural objects\, sketchbooks\, s
 tudies\, photos\, and notes from her personal archives\, showing the artis
 t’s perspective across multiple media forms. \n\nBank of America Museum
 s on Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on the first full we
 ekend of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of America Priv
 ate Bank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is your Bank of Americ
 a\, Merrill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and picture ID for acce
 ss. \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found here: https://about
 .bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
