BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://foundpoets.org/events", "Press Democrat": "https://foundpoets.org/events"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://foundpoets.org/events"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Found Poets! with headliner Jaz Sufi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T180000
UID:261014TVy5MjWhuE60CN2bPKtn1g
DESCRIPTION:San Ramon’s Poet Laureate Jaz Sufi filters her slam-honed in
 tensity through queer Iranian-American identity to spin you with spellbind
 ing storytelling.\n\nFound Poets! is about the entertainment of the spirit
  through performance poetry. From our development program grads to nationa
 lly acclaimed headliners\, Found Poets! is a challenging\, committed poetr
 y community dedicated to hosting a good night out.\n\n(Headliner)\n\n**Jaz
  Sufi**\n\nJaz Sufi (she/hers) is a queer Iranian-American poet and arts e
 ducator. She is the author of *Catalog of Shadows* (Game Over Books). Her 
 work has been published in Best New Poets\, Best of the Net\, AGNI\, Black
  Warrior Review\, Muzzle\, and elsewhere. She is a National Poetry Slam fi
 nalist and has received fellowships from Kundiman\, the Watering Hole\, an
 d New York University\, where she received her MFA. She is the current Poe
 t Laureate of San Ramon on occupied Ohlone land\, where she lives with her
  dog\, Apollo. IG: @calamityjaz www.jazsufi.com\n\n(Openers)\n\n**Grayson 
 Thompson**\n\nGrayson Thompson \\[he/him\\]\, a Black\, Jamaican-American\
 , queer transgender poet and therapist\, won Foglifter Press’s 2024 Star
 t A Riot! Chapbook Prize (June 2025) and Write Bloody Publishing’s 2024 
 Jack McCarthy Book Prize (September 2025) for *Sand Bodied Florida Boy.* I
 G: @graysonwritespoems www.graysonwritespoems.com\n\n**Ernesto Garay**\n\n
 Ernesto M. Garay is the author of a poetry collection\, *Reverberating Voi
 ces* (Flowersong Press\, 2022). Garay was LA Revista Bilingüe: La Voz’s
  Person of the Month in Sonoma County for March 2020\, and a Sonoma County
  Discovered Award Recipient in Literary Arts. He is Ethnic Studies faculty
  at Sierra College.\n\n**Anika Snyder**\n\nAnika Snyder was born and raise
 d in Northern California. She published her first book\, *Syllable Soccer*
 \, in 2025 and is soon to release her second. She has been published in Ef
 fable Press and performs her work regularly around Mendocino and Sonoma co
 unties. IG: @anika366\n\n**Gary Weiner**\n\nGary Weiner moved to Sonoma Co
 unty in 1973 and now resides in Sebastopol. A former working musician and 
 lawyer\, he released the full-length album *Released at Last* featuring N
 ina Gerber and exhibits photography in galleries across San Francisco and 
 Sebastopol. He is a prolific writer featured by the Sebastopol Center for 
 the Arts. IG: @gaweiner https://www.garyweinerarts.com/\n\n**Hosted by Jos
 h Windmiller + Original Giotis!**
LOCATION:The Big Easy
URL:https://foundpoets.org/events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108998370?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Ryan MacNeill & The Big Deal & JeConte & Archer Monk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
UID:2610203CXXQ-LGB02D-sriCmVeBg
DESCRIPTION:Experience a full day and night of live music in Point Reyes S
 tation as Ryan MacNeill & The Big Deal and JeConte take over the legendary
  Old Western Saloon on Saturday\, November 7.\n\nRyan MacNeill & The Big D
 eal kick things off from 4:00–7:00pm\, bringing their blend of Cosmic Am
 ericana\, rock & roll\, country\, and psychedelic roots music to one of We
 st Marin’s most iconic stages.\n\nFronted by Ryan MacNeill\, the band pa
 irs traditional songwriting with expansive guitar textures\, rich vocal ha
 rmonies\, driving basslines\, swirling organ\, and dynamic rhythms. Their 
 music moves easily between open-road Americana and exploratory\, psychedel
 ic jams—grounded in the traditions of American roots music while pushing
  well beyond them.\n\nThe evening continues from 8:00–11:00pm with JeCon
 te\, featuring rock & roll harmonica and special guest Archer Monk. The al
 l star band includes Matt Allard on organ\, Jono on bass\, Adam Bowers on 
 slide guitar\, and Andrew Tuckman on drums.\n\nSet in the heart of Point R
 eyes Station\, it’s an afternoon and evening of live music\, good times\
 , and West Marin character at the Old Western Saloon\, brought to you by W
 ild West Ferments.\n\nOld Western Saloon\n\n11201 CA-1\n\nPoint Reyes Stat
 ion\, CA 94956\n\nSaturday. November 7 2026\n\n4:00 – 7:00pm – Ryan Ma
 cNeill & the Big Deal\n\n8:00pm – 11:00pm – JeConte and Friends
LOCATION:Old Western Saloon
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108998370?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://musicinplace.org/event/easy-to-love-a-cole-porter-tribute-2/", "Press Democrat": "https://musicinplace.org/event/easy-to-love-a-cole-porter-tribute-2/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://musicinplace.org/event/easy-to-love-a-cole-porter-tribute-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Easy to Love – A Cole Porter Tribute
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
UID:260922jualAqY4Q0CAUN9vCFY2bA
DESCRIPTION:Experience the timeless sophistication and witty charm of one 
 of America’s greatest songwriters in this spectacular Cole Porter tribut
 e show. From unforgettable romantic ballads to sparkling\, upbeat show tun
 es\, this revue will showcase brilliant arrangements of Porter’s most be
 loved Broadway and Hollywood classics\, such as “Night and Day\,” “L
 et’s Do It\,” and “So In Love.” Join us for a dazzling musical jou
 rney that celebrates the sweeping melodies and clever lyrics that defined 
 an era of glamour. Don’t miss this captivating performance brought to li
 fe by world-class performers —secure your tickets today for an unforgett
 able afternoon of music!
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/easy-to-love-a-cole-porter-tribute-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
