ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/644_cs_library_workshop_tour.rev.178605768
 7.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:Join SRJC Librarian Jessica Harris and learn how to simplify c
 itations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the way\, score quick
  tips on finding credible research in the library and on the Web.NoodleToo
 ls helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliographies\, and offers n
 ote-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\, including the capabi
 lity to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Details: Extra Credit availa
 ble!This NoodleTools workshop will use APA and/or MLA style as live demo e
 xamples\, depending on the participants that register.Don't worry! Jessica
  will share how to use both MLA and APA. You're covered!You will learn how
  to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to s
 how how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check for errors.A
 long the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find credible researc
 h in the library and on the web.Check with your instructor to confirm the 
 citation style appropriate for your research assignment.Extra Credit: As s
 tudents\, you have the option to submit your instructor and course name wh
 en you register if you would like us to notify your instructor that you ha
 ve attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your ins
 tructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.Regis
 tration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)This workshop requires r
 egistration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.You will receive a
  confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your s
 pam folder if you do not see it.This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes ea
 rly to allow you time to log on.Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC stude
 nt conduct policy.Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how
  to join a Zoom meeting.Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
LAST-MODIFIED:20261005T200028Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://santarosa.libcal.com/calendar/workshops/noodletools_mla_11_9_2
 6
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Join SRJC Librarian Jessica Harris and learn 
 how to simplify citations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the 
 way\, score quick tips on finding credible research in the library and on 
 the Web.<br />NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and biblio
 graphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features
 \, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.<br />Workshop
  Details: Extra Credit available!<br />This NoodleTools workshop will use 
 APA and/or MLA style as live demo examples\, depending on the participants
  that register.<br />Don't worry! Jessica will share how to use both MLA a
 nd APA. You're covered!<br />You will learn how to sign up for an account 
 with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show how to create citations
 \, create a bibliography and check for errors.<br />Along the way\, you wi
 ll receive quick tips on how to find credible research in the library and 
 on the web.<br />Check with your instructor to confirm the citation style 
 appropriate for your research assignment.<br />Extra Credit: As students\,
  you have the option to submit your instructor and course name when you re
 gister if you would like us to notify your instructor that you have attend
 ed the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor o
 n an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.<br />Registra
 tion: (click "Begin Registration" button below)<br />This workshop require
 s registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.<br />You will 
 receive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Che
 ck your spam folder if you do not see it.<br />This Zoom workshop will ope
 n 10 minutes early to allow you time to log on.<br />Attendees are asked t
 o abide by SRJC student conduct policy.<br />Not familiar with Zoom? Watch
  this 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.<br />Have questions? C
 hat with an SRJC Librarian!
