UID:TKF/640bd014795edf4fa3769b14/586/29904270/0/0
DTSTART:20261109T203000Z
DTEND:20261109T220000Z
URL:https://tockify.com/rileystreet.art.com/detail/586/1794256200000
SUMMARY: Winsor & Newton Professional Watercolour Series - Class 2 of 3: 
 Watercolour Blooms – Landscape
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Ryan Martin\n\nDate: Monday\, November 9th\n\nTim
 e: 12:30PM-2PM\n\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n\nFree!\n\n\nClass 2 of 3: 
 Watercolour Blooms – Landscape -This is number two in a series of three c
 lasses using Winsor & Newton Professional Watercolour with artist Ryan Ma
 rtin. Attend all three to learn week-by-week from Ryan but none are prere
 quisites if your schedule does not allow. In this 90-minute session\, art
 ist Ryan will show you how to paint a luminous mountain and lake landscap
 e using wet-into-wet watercolour techniques and masking fluid to preserve
  crisp highlights. You’ll learn how to encourage watercolour blooms as pi
 gments spread\, soften\, and separate\, creating misty mountains\, glowin
 g skies\, and shimmering reflections. Winsor & Newton Art Masking Fluid w
 ill be used to save bright whites for snow\, light\, and sparkle\, making
  the scene feel alive and atmospheric. Minimal drawing experience is requ
 ired -this class is all about understanding timing\, water\, and pigment 
 to create beautiful\, expressive landscapes with confidence. All supplies
  are provided\, so you can try different pigments\, colors\, and brushes 
 and discover what you enjoy using. Ryan will also be available after clas
 s to answer questions and help you choose materials to keep exploring at 
 home.\n\n\nLimited seats available—reserve your spot today!\n\n\nRyan Mar
 tin lives and works in the San Francisco Bay Area where he attended the C
 alifornia College of the Arts. Through painting and drawing\, Martin crea
 tes surreal\, dream-like compositions of his subjects. He is influenced b
 y his Native American (Mexican/Seri) and Russian heritage through paintin
 g reinterpretations of war bonnets and kokoshniks haloing his subjects. M
 artin’s artwork has been highlighted by numerous media including The Advo
 cate\, Creative Boom\, The Art of Man and others. He has exhibited widely
  across the United States\, including the deYoung Museum\, Mark Wolfe Con
 temporary\, Modern Eden Gallery of San Francisco\, Elizabeth Houston Gall
 ery of NYC\, as well as numerous fairs including SCOPE\, Untitled Art in 
 Miami and Volta NY.\n\nWebsite: ryanmartinart.com http://ryanmartinart.co
 m • Instagram: @ryanmartinart
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Watercolor,Free-Demo
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/640bcf85795edf
 4fa3769ae5/6ad81bbc62b7c5607c3d3ccd/scaled_896.jpg
