DESCRIPTION:"Through portraiture\, we turn the camera toward dignity\, age
 ncy\, and self-representation. The women within these pages are dancers\, 
 artists\, bead workers\, teachers\, mothers\, daughters\, grandmothers\, l
 anguage keepers\, and land and water defenders. They are culture bearers\,
  but they are not defined by what they carry for others." — Julian Cook\
 , Co-Creator  A Portrait Series by Alexa LexMex Treviño (https://www.lexm
 exart.com/about) in collaboration with the SRJC Multicultural Museum.This 
 exhibit is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation
  Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.For more information\, visi
 t the SRJC Multicultural Museum website. (https://museum.santarosa.edu/eve
 nt/standing-her-power-portraits-beyond-colonial-frame)
